<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Great Arctic War - Arctic Cod Conflict, 2030</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;FONT size=6&gt;The Daily Global Courant &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;Friday, 21 June 2030&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;Royal Norwegian Navy moves to protect trawlers&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Arctic Cod Conflict causes deep freeze of Russo-Norwegian relations&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;OSLO, NORWAY (DGC) As the so called 'Arctic Cod Conflict' escalates, Norway has sent warships to protect trawlers operating in the disputed Russian Exclusive Economic Zone. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The warships are sailing alongside Norwegian trawlers now fishing in Box formation. The skippers said they would not return to the seas without naval protection from Russian gunboats and aircraft. Norwegian fishing vessels have been cruising the area since Russia unilaterally extended its fishing zone eight months ago. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;'The Navy is not going to stand idly by and see trawlers harassed,' said Karoline Barth-Westerdahl, a Norwegian state secretary from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. She said the warships would take 'appropriate action' if nessecary. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The&amp;nbsp;decision to send in the Navy was made three days ago by the Norwegian Defense Committee with Prime Minister Trond Giske present. The Russian ambassador in Oslo, Aleksei Tutko, said last&amp;nbsp;night that he was 'surprised and disappointed' by the move which he described as 'posturing'. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;'These resources belong to&amp;nbsp;the Russian people. The decision to allow Norwegian fishermen an annual 40,000 ton catch in our territorial waters is non-negotiable. The Norwegian demand of 120,000 tons is simply outrageous' said ambassador Tutko. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;========================================================================================================&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;NOTE:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This Scenario is an adaptation of the first campaign scenario of the now-unsupported game "Naval War: Arctic Circle" by Turbo Tape Games. Since that game is now effectively abandonware, with no support for over 6 years and the source code being released, I wanted to try and start an effort to remake the campaign in Command. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;If you own a copy of Naval War: Arctic Circle and are so inclinded to try and remake the scenarios, I encourage you to do so! &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Thanks for playing! &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;-Half Life Expert&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
